  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implement Cleanly and Independently**\n\nI\'m making good progress implementing the changes meticulously. I\'m prioritizing independent code generation, ensuring the virtual-stick control architecture and calibration parameters are reproduced accurately. It\'s crucial this implementation is separate and distinct, adhering to all guidelines. The code should be self-contained and accurate.\n\n\n**Detailing Configuration Changes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific file edits required. I\'m focusing on `/src/config/steering.ts`, ensuring the virtual-stick parameters are accurately translated and cleanly named with new constants. I\'m also addressing `/src/types/game.ts`, updating `GameSettings` and `FlightTelemetry` for precise virtual-stick telemetry. The goal is maintain a solid foundation for further development.\n\n\n**Refining Control Architecture**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the ship control flow. My focus is on `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`, specifically the independent virtual stick state. I am ensuring that the pointer lock functionality is preserved, and the decoupled self-centering virtual-stick state is carefully implemented. I am adding rate-independent exponential decay and optional linear deadzones to the input processing, along with keyboard arrow blending and thorough input snapshots. The next step is a clear separation of flight physics from mouse input in `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Core Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial flight dynamics and camera behavior. Specifically, I am implementing angular acceleration and damping, using quaternion multiplication for ship rotation relative to its local frame. I am ensuring that the ship\'s forward boresight aligns precisely with the new aiming direction. I have made updates to the camera and am removing lag to create a clean behind-ship chase. I also included impulse shake during combat, refined the camera follow, and implemented boost pullback and dynamic FOV. I am now updating GameScene and App components.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "AjL_auymMIq9vdIPtcLDuAw"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4882633554266596239"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * Centralized configuration for STARFALL\'s self-centering Virtual Stick\\n * mouse flight control and rotational flight response.\\n *\\n * Architectural notes:\\n * - Relative Pointer Lock mouse deltas (`movementX`, `movementY`) deflect a\\n *   normalized internal virtual stick in `[-maxStickDeflection, +maxStickDeflection]`\\n *   independently on X (yaw) and Y (pitch).\\n * - Internal stick range is completely decoupled from viewport dimensions,\\n *   aspect ratio, and any visual HUD reticle/ring radius.\\n * - When mouse movement stops, the virtual stick exponentially self-centers\\n *   at `stickSelfCenterRate` (1/s), smoothly tapering turn rate back to zero.\\n * - Ship turn rate (`yawSpeed`, `pitchSpeed`) governs maximum rotation speed\\n *   so airframe agility remains a true flight-model property.\\n */\\nexport const STEERING_CONFIG = {\\n  /**\\n   * Baseline normalized stick deflection per pixel of relative mouse movement.\\n   * 1 / 300 means 300 px of relative mouse travel reaches full 1.0 deflection\\n   * isotropically on both axes, independent of viewport size or aspect ratio.\\n   */\\n  baseMouseSensitivity: 1 / 300,\\n\\n  /** User mouse sensitivity multiplier applied to `baseMouseSensitivity` (1.0 = 300 px full travel) */\\n  mouseSensitivity: 1.0,\\n\\n  /** Exponential virtual-stick self-centering rate (1/s; half-life = ln(2) / 1.6 \342\211\210 0.433 s) */\\n  stickSelfCenterRate: 1.6,\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Normalized radial center deadzone (fraction of maxStickDeflection).\\n   * Default 0.0 ensures immediate, linear precision for small mouse movements.\\n   */\\n  deadzone: 0.0,\\n\\n  /** Maximum internal normalized stick deflection per axis */\\n  maxStickDeflection: 1.0,\\n\\n  /** Horizontal yaw turn-rate multiplier applied to ship `yawSpeed` */\\n  yawTurnRate: 1.0,\\n\\n  /** Vertical pitch turn-rate multiplier applied to ship `pitchSpeed` */\\n  pitchTurnRate: 1.0,\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Controlled maximum angular acceleration (rad/s^2) for the reference Interceptor hull.\\n   * High enough that virtual-stick deflection tracks with near-zero latency while smoothing\\n   * instantaneous digital step inputs (e.g., keyboard taps).\\n   */\\n  angularAcceleration: 36.0,\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Frame-rate-independent angular velocity tracking/damping rate (1/s) for the reference\\n   * Interceptor hull. Fast (~38 ms time constant) so angular velocity tracks the self-centering\\n   * virtual stick cleanly without double-damping lag or overshoot.\\n   */\\n  angularDamping: 26.0,\\n\\n  /** Reference ship angularDamping value used to scale hull agility proportionally */\\n  referenceShipAgility: 7.5,\\n\\n  /** Hard safety ceiling on angular rate multipliers relative to base ship turn speed */\\n  maxSafeTurnMultiplier: 1.8,\\n} as const;\\n\\nexport const STEERING_BOUNDS = {\\n  mouseSensitivity: { min: 0.3, max: 2.5 },\\n  stickSelfCenterRate: { min: 0.4, max: 4.0 },\\n  deadzone: { min: 0.0, max: 0.15 },\\n  maxStickDeflection: { min: 0.5, max: 1.0 },\\n  yawSensitivity: { min: 0.4, max: 1.8 },\\n  pitchSensitivity: { min: 0.4, max: 1.8 },\\n} as const;\\n\\n/**\\n * Purely visual HUD dimensions for the centered virtual-stick deflection indicator.\\n * Strictly separated from internal virtual-stick math and clamping.\\n */\\nexport const VISUAL_STICK_HUD = {\\n  /** Radius as a fraction of min(viewportWidth, viewportHeight) */\\n  ringRadiusFraction: 0.125,\\n  /** Minimum visual indicator ring radius in CSS pixels */\\n  minRingRadiusPx: 68,\\n  /** Maximum visual indicator ring radius in CSS pixels */\\n  maxRingRadiusPx: 118,\\n} as const;\\n\", \"Description\":\"Replace provisional rounded-rectangle & stacked curve parameters with centralized self-centering virtual-stick configuration calibrated to the reference architecture.\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/config/steering.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating centralized steering config\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update steering.ts\"}"
