  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nThe user pivoted from the earlier NEON ORBIT virtual-stick pass (which was canceled and rolled back) to an **Emergency Flight Feel Recovery & Stabilization Pass** for STARFALL:\n- **Explicitly chosen flight model**: **B \342\200\224 Traditional Arcade Space Combat** (direct, responsive, low-latency mouse steering \342\200\224 NOT a sluggish or self-centering virtual joystick).\n- **Target feel**:\n  - Relative mouse movement (`movementX`, `movementY`) directly drives yaw and pitch steering intent.\n  - Small mouse movements produce small, precise turns; larger movements produce stronger turns; ship responds immediately with low input latency.\n  - Smooth continuous turning, easy target tracking, fast large directional changes, and **no unwanted drifting or uncontrollable rotation after the player stops moving the mouse**.\n  - **No sluggish virtual joystick behavior, no virtual-joystick self-centering fights, no excessive deadzone, no excessive inertia/smoothing, no stacked sensitivity curves or duplicated multipliers.**\n  - Controlled maximum angular velocity; horizontal (yaw) and vertical (pitch) sensitivity independently adjustable; consistent response across frame rates.\n- **Aim Boundary requirement**:\n  - Keep a configurable centered rounded-rectangle aiming boundary (`width: 30%` of viewport width, `height: 35%` of viewport height, rounded rectangle, centered).\n  - **CRITICAL**: Do NOT let boundary size act as a hidden sensitivity multiplier or create excessive sensitivity. Simplify its interaction with the flight controller so it defines the aiming region cleanly without conflicting with direct arcade steering or breaking continuous mouse input.\n- **Pointer Lock requirement (CRITICAL)**:\n  - Preserve STARFALL\'s working Pointer Lock fix in `src/engine/InputManager.ts` (`document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget`, pure `movementX`/`movementY`, zero cursor recentering, no `clientX`/`clientY` dependency, physical screen edges never interrupt steering, warp-spike filter `> 500px`, no double-processing).\n- **Camera requirement**:\n  - Third-person chase camera follows smoothly, responds quickly to directional changes, avoids excessive trailing, and avoids competing with ship rotation.\n- **Scope**:\n  - Smallest possible set of focused changes to mouse input, steering config, flight controller, camera controller, HUD aim boundary/reticle, and directly related settings.\n  - Do NOT redesign combat, weapons, bots, missions, progression, or unrelated UI/visual design.\n- **Required Deliverables & Acceptance Tests**:\n  - Test the **actual browser game** (on `http://localhost:3000`) verifying all 11 acceptance criteria: small movements = precise turns, larger movements = stronger turns, immediate response, no excessive input lag, no unwanted drifting after input stops, no uncontrollable rotation, smooth predictable target tracking, stable camera follow, consistent behavior across frame rates, Pointer Lock working at physical screen edges, and boost intact.\n  - Final report covering: (1) root causes of poor flight feel, (2) files changed, (3) old behaviors removed/corrected, (4) final sensitivity & angular velocity settings, (5) how input latency was controlled, (6) actual browser test results, (7) remaining problems.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Skills read**:\n  - `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/threejs/references/interaction.md`\n- **Completed inspections (current on-disk state verified right before handoff)**:\n  - `/src/config/steering.ts` (75 lines) \342\200\224 currently in original pre-recovery state (virtual joystick params: `deadzone: 0.06`, `precisionSensitivity: 0.85`, `responseCurve: 1.35`, `angularAcceleration: 18.0`, `angularDamping: 14.0`, `stoppingDampingBoost: 1.25`).\n  - `/src/engine/InputManager.ts` (326 lines) \342\200\224 currently in original pre-recovery state (clean Pointer Lock + raw `mouseDeltaX`/`mouseDeltaY` per-frame accumulation; no virtual-stick state).\n  - `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` (616 lines) \342\200\224 currently in original pre-recovery state (still accumulates persistent `joystickX`/`joystickY` that never stop turning when mouse stops, clamps to rounded rect, applies `evaluateVirtualJoystick`, applies `GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD = 0.22` / `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD = 0.16`, and **imports deleted `./AimBoundary`**).\n  - `/src/engine/CameraController.ts` (193 lines) \342\200\224 currently in original pre-recovery state (contains sign-inverted `lagX = clamp(-flight.yawVelocity * 0.5, -1.35, 1.35)` and `lagY = clamp(flight.pitchVelocity * 0.4, -0.95, 0.95)`).\n  - Earlier in the session (prior to user cancel/rollback), also read: `/src/config/ships.ts`, `/src/types/game.ts`, `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx`, `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, `/src/App.tsx`, `/src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`, `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts`, `/package.json`. (Verify current state of `ships.ts`, `types/game.ts`, `FlightHUD.tsx`, `SettingsPanel.tsx`, `GameScene.tsx`, `App.tsx` if needed \342\200\224 rollback likely reverted them alongside the 4 inspected files.)\n- **Deleted by user**:\n  - `/src/engine/AimBoundary.ts` was explicitly deleted by the user. Consequently, existing imports of `AimBoundary` in `FlightController.ts`, `FlightHUD.tsx`, and `SettingsPanel.tsx` are currently broken until updated or replaced with a minimal pure-geometry boundary helper.\n- **No edits have been made yet** for the new Emergency Flight Feel Recovery (Traditional Arcade Space Combat) pass.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\nRoot causes identified in the current STARFALL implementation (`FlightController.ts`, `steering.ts`, `CameraController.ts`, `FlightHUD.tsx`):\n1. **Persistent non-stopping virtual joystick accumulation (`FlightController.ts` lines 367\342\200\223377)**:\n   - `joystickX += mouseDeltaX * inputScale` accumulates mouse motion into a persistent offset that NEVER returns to zero when the player stops moving the mouse. The ship continues spinning indefinitely after input stops, forcing the player to manually reverse-drag to find the center deadzone.\n2. **Hidden sensitivity distortion from the 30%\303\22735% rounded-rectangle boundary (`FlightController.ts` lines 340\342\200\223389)**:\n   - At 1280\303\227720, `halfW = 192px` (30% W) and `halfH = 126px` (35% H), while `resScale` scaled by `vh / 720`. Dividing displacement by `halfW` / `halfH` turned the aim boundary size (`joystickRadius`) and viewport aspect ratio into hidden, asymmetric sensitivity multipliers (vertical travel was 1.52\303\227 more sensitive than horizontal travel, and shrinking the boundary boosted sensitivity!).\n3. **Stacked deadzone + nonlinear curve + precision shaping + duplicated multipliers**:\n   - `deadzone = 0.06` ignored micro-corrections.\n   - `pow(u, 1.35) * (0.85 + 0.15 * smoothstep(u))` crushed small inputs and ramped sharply near the outer edge (unexpected sensitivity acceleration).\n   - Stacked `mouseSensitivity` \303\227 `resScale` \303\227 `1/boundaryRadius` \303\227 curve \303\227 `yawSensitivity`/`pitchSensitivity` \303\227 `profile.yawSpeed`/`pitchSpeed`.\n4. **Excessive angular inertia / acceleration lag (`FlightController.ts` lines 155\342\200\223179, 426\342\200\223443)**:\n   - `angularAcceleration = 18.0`, `angularDamping = 14.0` combined with indirect joystick displacement created noticeable sluggishness and lag between mouse motion and ship response.\n5. **Sign-inverted lateral camera lag fighting turns (`CameraController.ts` lines 71\342\200\22372)**:\n   - In STARFALL\'s coordinate system (`Forward = -Z, Right = +X, Up = +Y`), yawing RIGHT produces **negative** `yawVelocity`.\n   - `lagX = -flight.yawVelocity * 0.5` becomes **positive** (`+X`), shifting the camera *right* (toward the inside of the turn), fighting natural outside-arc chase follow and making ship alignment feel unnatural/competing with rotation.\n6. **Large off-nose weapon gimbal offset (`FlightController.ts` lines 143\342\200\223145, 294\342\200\223300)**:\n   - `GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD = 0.22` (~12.6\302\260), `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD = 0.16` (~9.2\302\260) swung weapon convergence and the boresight reticle far away from the ship nose during turns.\n7. **Coordinate & sign conventions verified**:\n   - Ship local frame: `Forward = -Z`, `Right = +X`, `Up = +Y`.\n   - Local `+Y` rotation turns nose **LEFT** \342\206\222 moving mouse RIGHT (`mouseDeltaX > 0`) must produce **negative** `yawVelocity`.\n   - Local `+X` rotation pitches nose **UP** \342\206\222 moving mouse UP (`mouseDeltaY < 0`, `invertY = false`) must produce **positive** `pitchVelocity` (and `invertY = true` flips it).\n   - Local `+Z` rotation rolls **LEFT** (CCW looking down `-Z`) \342\206\222 `KeyA` (`rollLeft`) produces positive `rollVelocity`, `KeyD` (`rollRight`) produces negative `rollVelocity`.\n8. **Environment facts for browser testing**:\n   - Dev server runs on `http://localhost:3000/` (returned HTTP 200).\n   - Chromium headless shell is available at `/ms-playwright/chrome-headless-shell-linux64` (symlink to `/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1247/chrome-headless-shell-linux64`), and `/ms-playwright/skill` exists (playwright is NOT in local `node_modules`).\n   - `App.tsx` exposes `window.__STARFALL_DIAG__` in DEV mode (`getFlight`, `getInput`, `getTelemetry`, `getSettings`, `getPhase`) which enables direct quantitative verification in real Chromium browser tests.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Canceled turn / abandoned approach**:\n  - In the previous turn, an independently written NEON ORBIT self-centering virtual-stick model (`1/300` px sensitivity, `1.6/s` exponential self-centering) was implemented and tested in Node, but the user canceled before browser testing and explicitly rejected virtual-joystick / self-centering behavior in favor of **Model B: Traditional Arcade Space Combat (direct relative mouse steering)**. Do NOT reintroduce virtual-stick accumulation or self-centering.\n- **Unresolved broken build state (expected right now)**:\n  - The user deleted `/src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`. Because the previous turn was canceled/reverted, `FlightController.ts`, `FlightHUD.tsx`, and `SettingsPanel.tsx` still import from `AimBoundary`. This must be resolved cleanly during the recovery pass (either recreate a lightweight pure-geometry `AimBoundary.ts` strictly for the configurable 30%\303\22735% visual/aim region with zero sensitivity coupling, or place that minimal geometry helper where needed and remove all dead curve/joystick imports).\n- **Temp directory cleanup**:\n  - `/tmp/neon-orbit` was cloned during the earlier turn; remove `/tmp/neon-orbit` if desired (outside workspace).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Workspace root is `/app/applet` (file tool paths start with `/`, e.g., `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`).\n- `npm run lint` executes `tsc --noEmit`; `npm run build` executes `vite build`.\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (restart with `restart_dev_server` after compiling if needed).\n- `InputManager.ts` is already clean, minimal, and preserves the exact Pointer Lock fix (`document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget`, `movementX`/`movementY`, warp-spike filter `> 500px`, single-consumption per frame via `consumeSnapshot()`). It likely needs **zero or minimal changes**!\n- Key design for **Direct Traditional Arcade Mouse Steering (Model B)**:\n  - **Direct rate steering from relative mouse movement** (zero persistent joystick spin, zero self-centering fight):\n    - Convert relative per-frame mouse delta (`mouseDeltaX`, `mouseDeltaY`) into a frame-rate-independent angular rate command:\n      - Rate = `(mouseDelta / safeDt) * baseMouseRadPerPx * mouseSensitivity` (or equivalently, direct angular displacement `deltaAngle = -mouseDelta * radPerPx * mouseSensitivity * axisSens`, clamped by `maxAngularSpeed * safeDt`, smoothed lightly via fast exponential velocity tracking `angularDamping` so motion is silky-smooth with ~1\342\200\2232 frame latency and stops crisply when the mouse stops!).\n      - **Check frame-rate consistency carefully!**\n        - If you move the mouse `100 px` over `0.5 s` (i.e., `200 px/s`):\n          - Instantaneous mouse velocity is `mouseVelX = input.mouseDeltaX / safeDt` (px/s).\n          - Desired angular velocity is `targetYaw = clamp(-mouseVelX * baseRadPerPx * mouseSensitivity * yawSens, -maxYawSpeed, maxYawSpeed)`.\n          -Wait: think about discrete mouse polling (e.g., 125 Hz mouse on 144 Hz display where some frames have `mouseDelta = 0` and adjacent frames have `2\303\227` delta)! A light, fast exponential filter on angular velocity (e.g., `dampingRate ~ 22\342\200\22328 /s`, \317\204 \342\211\210 35\342\200\22345 ms, or short smoothing time constant) smooths out discrete mouse polling ticks into silky continuous turning WITHOUT feeling laggy, AND integrates exact total angle `\342\210\253 targetYaw dt = -\316\243 mouseDeltaX * baseRadPerPx * sens` independently of 30 / 60 / 120 / 144 FPS (as long as not saturated at `maxYawSpeed`)!\n          - Verify mathematically:\n            - Small 10 px move \342\206\222 small ~2\302\260\342\200\2233\302\260 precise turn, stops cleanly within ~0.1s, ZERO lingering drift!\n            - Continuous drag at steady speed \342\206\222 smooth, continuous turning at proportional angular rate!\n            - Fast flick \342\206\222 reaches controlled `maxYawSpeed` / `maxPitchSpeed` ceiling cleanly without uncontrollable spin!\n            - Stopping mouse \342\206\222 `mouseVel = 0` \342\206\222 `targetYaw = 0` \342\206\222 fast exponential decay (`e^(-24 * dt)`) brings angular velocity smoothly to exact `0` in ~0.12s (zero drift, zero snapping)!\n            - Moving mouse at 30 FPS vs 60 FPS vs 144 FPS \342\206\222 identical total rotation for the same pixel travel and identical steady-state turn rate for the same px/s!\n  - **Clean, non-interfering 30%\303\22735% Centered Rounded-Rectangle Aim Boundary**:\n    - Restore a minimal, clean `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts` (or geometry helper) strictly defining the configurable centered 30% W \303\227 35% H rounded-rectangle region (`aimBoundaryWidth: 0.30`, `aimBoundaryHeight: 0.35`, `aimBoundaryCornerRadius: 0.30`).\n    - Use it for the **visual HUD aiming frame** and (optionally) a subtle visual/aim reticle lead offset proportional to current angular rate / clamped smoothly inside the rounded-rectangle boundary \342\200\224 **NEVER dividing mouse deltas by boundary size and NEVER coupling boundary dimensions to turn sensitivity**.\n    - That way: changing boundary size never alters mouse sensitivity, continuous 360\302\260 Pointer Lock turning is never interrupted, and the aiming reticle visually stays neatly inside the centered 30%\303\22735% rounded rectangle!\n  - **CameraController**:\n    - Remove the sign-inverted `lagX = -flight.yawVelocity * 0.5` / `lagY` offset that fought turns.\n    - Keep crisp, responsive chase follow (`posLambda` ~ `13.5\342\200\22315`, `rotLambda` ~ `18\342\200\22320`, `upAlpha` ~ `13.5`, scaled by `cameraSensitivity`) so the camera tracks directional changes quickly with minimal trailing while preserving cinematic feel and boost FOV/pullback.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Inspect remaining files to confirm exact current post-rollback state** (quick parallel `view_file` on `/src/config/ships.ts`, `/src/types/game.ts`, `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx`, `/src/App.tsx`).\n2. **Design & implement minimal recovery edits**:\n   - `/src/config/steering.ts`: Clean centralized direct-arcade steering configuration (`baseRadiansPerPixel`, `mouseSensitivity: 1.0`, `yawSensitivity: 1.0`, `pitchSensitivity: 1.0`, `deadzone: 0.0` (or minimal configurable noise threshold), `angularSmoothing` / `angularDamping` (~24\342\200\22328/s), `maxYawSpeed` / `maxPitchSpeed` / `maxSafeTurnMultiplier`, plus decoupled visual `aimBoundaryWidth: 0.30`, `aimBoundaryHeight: 0.35`, `aimBoundaryCornerRadius: 0.30`). Zero stacked response curves or `precisionSensitivity` distortions.\n   - `/src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`: Recreate a minimal, pure-geometry rounded-rectangle boundary module (centered 30% W \303\227 35% H, corner radius 30%) strictly for HUD framing & bounded visual reticle positioning \342\200\224 zero response curves, zero sensitivity scaling.\n   - `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`: Keep Pointer Lock fix 100% intact (verify no changes needed or minimal cleanup only; ensure zero double-processing).\n   - `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`:\n     - Replace persistent virtual-joystick accumulation with **direct relative mouse-delta arcade steering**: `mouseVel = mouseDelta / safeDt`, scaled by one centralized `baseRadiansPerPixel * mouseSensitivity` + independent `yawSensitivity` / `pitchSensitivity`, clamped to controlled ship max angular velocity (`profile.yawSpeed` / `profile.pitchSpeed` \303\227 safe cap), with light fast exponential damping (`~24\342\200\22328 /s`) so there is low latency, smooth continuous turning, crisp stop on zero input, and zero drift.\n     - Keep arrow-key steering, independent A/D roll, boost, linear thrust, and lateral grip untouched.\n     - Align `getAimDirectionWorld` cleanly along ship forward boresight (or tiny bounded visual aim alignment without erratic gimbal swing) and map HUD aim indicator smoothly within the 30%\303\22735% rounded-rectangle boundary (centered smoothly when angular velocity is zero).\n   - `/src/engine/CameraController.ts`: Fix the sign-inverted `lagX`/`lagY` offset and tune chase camera follow (`posLambda`, `rotLambda`, `upAlpha`) for fast, crisp, stable tracking without excessive trailing or competing with ship rotation.\n   - `/src/config/ships.ts`, `/src/types/game.ts`, `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`: Cleanly align settings (remove misleading stacked curve/joystick-radius sensitivity coupling; bump settings storage key if needed so stale v6 curve/deadzone values don\'t pollute recovery defaults) and fix all imports of `AimBoundary`.\n3. **Verify compilation & linting**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together and fix any TypeScript/Vite issues.\n   - Restart dev server if needed (`restart_dev_server`).\n4. **Run quantitative simulation tests + REAL BROWSER TESTS (mandatory per Sections 8\342\200\22310)**:\n   - First run a headless `tsx` verification testing frame-rate consistency (30, 60, 120, 144 FPS), small vs large mouse movements, stopping drift (must settle to 0 quickly), max angular velocity capping, and boost preservation.\n   - Then test the **actual running browser game** on `http://localhost:3000` using headless Chromium (`/ms-playwright/chrome-headless-shell-linux64` via CDP or Playwright from `/ms-playwright/skill` or a lightweight Node CDP script using built-in `WebSocket` / `ws` \342\200\224 check what\'s in `/ms-playwright/skill` first!).\n   - In the real browser test: launch a mission, engage Pointer Lock on the `<canvas>`, dispatch relative mouse movement sequences (small movements, large sweeps, continuous edge-crossing sweeps, abrupt stop, return/reverse, boost + turn), inspect `window.__STARFALL_DIAG__` (flight quaternion, yaw/pitch velocities, heading/pitch degrees, boost speed/energy, Pointer Lock ownership, HUD reticle/boundary bounds), capture screenshots if helpful, and verify zero console/page errors.\n5. **Cleanup**: Remove `/tmp/neon-orbit` and any temporary test scripts outside the repo.\n6. **Final Report**: Deliver a concise, technically precise report matching Section 10\'s exact 7-point checklist based ONLY on actually verified tests.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **User explicitly chose Model B (Traditional Arcade Space Combat)**: direct relative mouse steering, low latency, no sluggish virtual joystick, no self-centering fights, no drifting after stopping.\n- **Preserve the working Pointer Lock fix**: never touch/break `document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget`, `movementX`/`movementY`, zero cursor recentering, edge-continuity.\n- **Smallest possible changes**: do not touch combat, weapons, bots, missions, progression, audio, or visual design.\n- **Keep configurable 30% W \303\227 35% H centered rounded-rectangle aim boundary**, decoupled from turn sensitivity.\n- **Never claim browser testing passed unless actually executed in the browser** against the live app.\n- **Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`** on the final verification pass before concluding.\n</summary>"
