  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Clean Execution**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` both succeeded without issue on their initial runs. Now, I\'m moving on to rigorous verification. I\'m focusing on deterministic quantitative simulation tests within Node, using `npx tsx`, to assess all physics and math acceptance criteria. The first test will involve a small mouse movement (5px, 1 frame).\n\n\n**Validating Movement Behaviors**\n\nI\'m now deep in the validation phase, focusing on precise movement characteristics. I\'m verifying responsiveness to both small and large mouse movements, ensuring capped angular rates during rapid flicks. Immediate decay to zero angular velocity after mouse stops and frame-rate consistency across multiple FPS values are high priorities. Further, I\'m confirming aim boundary decoupling and independent sensitivity controls. I\'m also looking into chase follow stability and the preservation of boost behavior.\n\n\n"
