  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Results**\n\nI\'m incredibly relieved we ran the real browser test! It immediately revealed a crucial omission: the `aimBoundaryScale` setting. Also, I see the old `pitchSensitivity` value (0.9) is still present. This clearly identifies areas needing immediate attention in the configuration.\n\n\n**Investigating the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve got it! The `widthPx` being NaN and `aimBoundaryScale` undefined stemmed from a stale `ships.ts` module or a cached Vite dev server. The `FlightHUD.tsx` was reading `aimBoundaryScale`, and if it was undefined, `computeRoundedRectBoundary` produced NaN! This points to the old configuration, indicating a reload failure and stale cache. My focus shifts to the dev server\'s reloading process.\n\n\n**Confirming Native Success**\n\nOkay, so the `ships.ts` module or a dev server cache was definitely the primary cause! Crucially, the real browser test confirmed Chromium\'s native pointer lock success on the canvas. I see the input manager caught and filtered that -640,-360 lock-warp spike!  Now, I\'ll be hardening `computeRoundedRectBoundary` and will never repeat this issue again, even if a stale setting is passed. Also, I\'ll explore more deeply into the dev server reloading for stability.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "LDX_asS1Mdmfz7IPjtv-mAc"
    tool_calls {
