  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Outcome**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased to report zero console errors in `task-132`! Furthermore, the settings are impeccable: mouseSensitivity, yawSensitivity, pitchSensitivity, and aimBoundaryScale are all at 1. This is a solid foundation, and the aim boundary is behaving exactly as intended.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Animation Frames**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! My tests were being hampered by SwiftShader\'s slow rendering. Sleeping fixed intervals didn\'t work. Now, I\'m synchronizing with `requestAnimationFrame` to ensure my browser tests run in sync with the WebGL rendering, instead of racing ahead of the slow frame times. This should result in more accurate and meaningful results.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "izX_atH_NqrUz7IPjL6sgAc"
